/** User manual — Golden A/S edition (staff and administrators).   GAS-CP-R20-002 */
return [
  'title' => 'Customer Portal — User Manual (Golden A/S staff and administrators)',
  'lede'  => 'How Golden A/S runs its projects, tickets, work orders, service reports, timesheets, offers, contacts and settings in the portal — and what each role may do.',
  'sections' => [
    ['id' => 'roles', 'title' => 'Roles and access', 'body' => [
      'Three kinds of account exist. Owner / customer accounts belong to a customer and see only that customer\'s vessels and projects, and only external items. Golden A/S staff accounts see every customer; what they may do is refined by a Golden A/S role (Settings › Golden A/S roles) and a discipline. Administrators have every right, including the Settings pages, deletions, imports and the file archive.',
      ['fig' => 'roles.svg', 'cap' => 'What each kind of account sees and does'],
      'Browser protection (Settings › Login history › Content-Security-Policy): the portal tells the browser to run only its own scripts (every inline script carries a one-time nonce), to load resources only from the portal itself (plus the weather service of the clocks), never to embed the portal inside another site and never to send a form elsewhere; camera access is allowed for photos, microphone, location and payment APIs are off. Keep it Enforced; switch to Report only for a day if a page misbehaves after a customisation — violations are then written to storage/csp.log instead of being blocked.',
      'Sessions (Settings › Login history › Sessions & sign-in policy): a session ends after the idle time-out (30 minutes by default), after the maximum duration (10 hours by default) even while in use, and when the browser is closed — every open portal tab keeps a window marker alive, and a page that opens without a fresh one (browser closed and reopened, tabs restored by Edge or Chrome, the address typed later) drops the session; a new tab opened while another one is open stays signed in. A session is bound to the browser it was opened in (and optionally to the network): a cookie copied elsewhere is refused and logged as "Session closed (other device)". Administrators can sign any account out of every browser from Portal accounts (⎋ Sign out everywhere); everybody can do the same for their own account under My account › My sessions. Every policy event is in the login history (Session expired, Session closed (other device), Signed out everywhere, Signed out (browser closed)).',
      ['ul' => ['Rich text: every multi-line text box (notes, descriptions, comments, remarks, report texts) has a toolbar — B, I, U, bulleted and numbered lists, with Ctrl+B / I / U and Enter continuing a list. The marks are portable (**bold**, _italic_, __underline__, "- " and "1. " lines): formatted on screen, clean text with • bullets in PDF and Word, unchanged in Excel exports and e-mails. E-mail templates stay plain.', 'Internal vs external: every note, comment and file has a visibility. Internal items are never shown to owners — use them for anything that is not for the customer\'s eyes.', 'Drafts (work orders, service reports, owner-approval documents) are invisible to owners until submitted.', 'Financial data (offer amounts, invoicing, timesheet invoicing) is shown to a Golden A/S role only when the administrator has ticked Financial data — visible for that role.', 'Staff cannot sign in without two-factor authentication unless the administrator has exempted the account.']],
    ]],
    ['id' => 'dashboard', 'title' => 'Dashboard and attention list', 'body' => [
      'The clock strip under the top bar shows UTC, Greece (home), the UAE, the United Kingdom, Italy, the Netherlands, Germany and Dallas in 24-hour time on every page, with a −1d / +1d mark when a zone is on another calendar day. The Athens clock shows a weather badge; click any city for sunrise / sunset, daylight length, the conditions now, today\'s minimum / maximum, rain chance, wind and the hourly forecast (Open-Meteo, refreshed every 30 minutes by the browser). The staff dashboard shows the whole fleet: progress by sub-project, open tickets, offers awaiting owners, approvals pending, the hours booked this week, and the attention list — everything assigned to you or unassigned, oldest first. Each figure opens the corresponding list already filtered.',
      ['fig' => 'g-dashboard.jpg', 'cap' => 'The staff dashboard'],
